content.text:
No new errors. Good.

Need validate HUD after level. Simulate 10s maybe. Use eval to add XP? Could call H.collectSoul? But easier use H.state.xp=20 and trigger? Need test level overlay by calling H.openLevelUp. We'll later.

Let's inspect game screen after 30s simulation with movement around. Could write an automated bot in page:
```
const H=__HORDE__.H, s=H.state;
for (i=0;i<3600;i++){ set keys toward nearest survivor; H.updateWorld(1/60); H.updateCamera(1/60) }
```
But this may trigger level-up and mode='levelup' stopping update. We can auto-select random upgrade when mode levelup:
```
if (s.mode==='levelup') { H.chooseUpgrade(H.currentChoices[0]); }
```
This would test cards.
Also core movement. Need mind H.updateWorld uses state.mode playing; choose upgrade sets playing. Good.
- direct key via H.input.keys.add('d') etc.
- each step target nearest survivor direction. 
- Use `for` loop with H.updateWorld(1/60) and H.updateCamera.
- Render after.
- Need not trigger actual game clock. Good.
- Could run 60 sec to see boss. But browser script loop heavy but okay. Need handle game over.
